// `--bare` must still refuse read_file, by name.
//
// The refused-host-services list `read_file` used to sit on was protecting the
// machine-only target: --bare hands `main` the machine as a `Raw` and there is
// no host behind it to read a file from. Lowering read_file for the HOSTED
// target must not quietly give --bare a filesystem too -- that is the
// permissive direction, and the permissive direction is the worse one to be
// wrong in.
//
// This is a separate file from host_read_file.mere because a --bare program has
// to have a top-level `main` taking a Raw. Without one the compiler refuses it
// for THAT reason, and a check that reads the refusal without reading its
// reason passes while testing nothing -- which is exactly what the first
// version of this gate did.
let main = fn (m: Raw) -> read_file "anything";
